BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 642.00 Td (Abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 622.00 Td (During long-context inference the key-value cache, not the model weights, dominates GPU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 609.00 Td (memory. We present SQUEEZE, a tuning-free method that stores the cache in two bits per) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 596.00 Td (number. Keys are quantized per channel and values per token, following the structure of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 583.00 Td (their outliers, and a small window of recent tokens is kept in full precision. SQUEEZE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 570.00 Td (reduces KV cache memory by 5.3 times and raises decoding throughput by 3.1 times with an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 557.00 Td (average accuracy loss of 0.4 points on LongSuite.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 537.00 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 517.00 Td (For a 7B model serving a batch of 16 requests at 32K tokens, the cache needs 256 GB in half) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 504.00 Td (precision, far more than the weights. Quantizing the cache is attractive because it needs no) Tj ET
