BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 438.00 Td (We inspected the cached keys and values of every layer of three model families. Keys and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 425.00 Td (values behave differently. In the keys, a few key channels carry outliers whose magnitude is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 412.00 Td (ten to fifty times the median, and they are the same channels for every token. Values show) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 399.00 Td (no fixed outlier channels, but their error matters per token because the attention output is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 386.00 Td (a weighted sum of value rows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 366.00 Td (This motivates quantizing keys per channel, so that each outlier channel gets its own scale,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 353.00 Td (and quantizing values per token, so that the error of each value row is bounded. Quantizing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 340.00 Td (keys per token, as earlier work did, spreads one outlier's range over the whole row and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 327.00 Td (leaves the other channels with almost no resolution.) Tj ET
